1
00:00:00,185 --> 00:00:04,492
An interaction should be easier to deliver than a collection of screenshots.

2
00:00:04,492 --> 00:00:09,516
TapeWeave turns a small behavior into a runnable package: something a creator can share,

3
00:00:09,516 --> 00:00:12,746
an application can consume, and a reviewer can check.

4
00:00:12,746 --> 00:00:14,541
Here is the working product.

5
00:00:15,652 --> 00:00:18,125
I start with charge and release.

6
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:21,009
Generate the work, charge once, then trigger.

7
00:00:21,009 --> 00:00:22,246
The lamp lights.

8
00:00:22,246 --> 00:00:25,955
Trigger again without recharging, and no effect is requested.

9
00:00:25,955 --> 00:00:31,725
The trace exposes the old state, inputs, next state, and request, instead of hiding

10
00:00:31,725 --> 00:00:33,785
the rule behind an animation.

11
00:00:34,896 --> 00:00:39,233
The package contains the rule, its digest, and the receiving scene.

12
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:43,175
I copy it into the receiving field and validate it.

13
00:00:43,175 --> 00:00:45,146
That starts a fresh session.

14
00:00:45,146 --> 00:00:49,088
After two actions, I refresh and restore the saved execution.

15
00:00:49,088 --> 00:00:53,030
Recovery recomputes the steps rather than trusting a displayed score.

16
00:00:54,141 --> 00:00:58,348
Now I alter the digest in a copy of the package.

17
00:00:58,348 --> 00:01:01,408
Import fails, and the current session stays unchanged.

18
00:01:01,408 --> 00:01:04,851
This is a content consistency check, not publisher authentication.

19
00:01:04,851 --> 00:01:10,206
Ordinary shared truth tables remain available as a fair comparison; we do not claim

20
00:01:10,206 --> 00:01:12,119
that circuits are automatically better.

21
00:01:13,241 --> 00:01:16,964
The same behavior also runs in two application examples.

22
00:01:16,964 --> 00:01:21,515
One reveals a story; the other issues a local commemorative stamp.

23
00:01:21,515 --> 00:01:23,997
Each has separate state and resources.

24
00:01:23,997 --> 00:01:27,307
An effective request cannot bypass the stamp inventory.

25
00:01:27,307 --> 00:01:32,685
Both examples are built by us; they are not presented as independent adoption.

26
00:01:33,807 --> 00:01:36,864
There is also a real X Layer integration.

27
00:01:36,864 --> 00:01:42,212
An account abstraction wallet deployed the host through Create X, then opened and completed

28
00:01:42,212 --> 00:01:43,358
both four-step cards.

29
00:01:43,358 --> 00:01:46,415
Eleven published transactions cover deployment and both runs.

30
00:01:46,415 --> 00:01:51,763
The interface separates this historical evidence from a fresh public R P C read.

31
00:01:52,874 --> 00:01:56,729
I read the charge card session from the public network.

32
00:01:56,729 --> 00:02:02,126
Its final result is two training points, one opened door, and one remaining key.

33
00:02:02,126 --> 00:02:04,824
The alternating card produces a different outcome.

34
00:02:04,824 --> 00:02:08,294
Reviewers can download the evidence and rerun the verifier.

35
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:11,763
A read-only result does not prove a new signature.

36
00:02:12,874 --> 00:02:15,922
The web wallet flows require explicit confirmation.

37
00:02:15,922 --> 00:02:22,017
The account abstraction entry checks deployed account code and native call capabilities, preserves unknown

38
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:25,065
requests, and verifies successful User Operation events.

39
00:02:25,065 --> 00:02:28,112
This recording does not stage a signature.

40
00:02:28,112 --> 00:02:34,207
Full independent User Operation simulation and real browser A A acceptance remain separate milestones.

41
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:41,180
TapeWeave is a working interaction delivery prototype, not a marketplace or a universal automation

42
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:41,599
engine.

43
00:02:41,599 --> 00:02:46,623
The next test is independent developer integration, measured against ordinary shared code.

44
00:02:46,623 --> 00:02:51,647
Try the live demo, inspect the source, and reproduce the mainnet evidence.

45
00:02:51,647 --> 00:02:53,321
Create a behavior once.

46
00:02:53,321 --> 00:02:56,252
Make its meaning clear wherever it runs.
